Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: avoid returning a WCID for another RX band

When a received frame reports a band different from the descriptor WCID,
look up the peer link for that band. If the VIF no longer has such a link,
return NULL instead of falling back to the original WCID. That fallback
attributes the frame to the wrong link during link reconfiguration.

Also handle a matching VIF link with no corresponding peer link explicitly.

---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -49,10 +49,10 @@
 			continue;
 
 		msta_link = mt7996_sta_link(msta, i);
-		break;
-	}
-
-	return &msta_link->wcid;
+		return msta_link ? &msta_link->wcid : NULL;
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
 }
 
 bool mt7996_mac_wtbl_update(struct mt7996_dev *dev, int idx, u32 mask)
